-- title:
--   SL₂(ℤ)-invariance plus holomorphic q-expansion forces constancy
-- statement:
--   Let $F \colon \mathfrak{H} \to \mathbb{C}$ be a function on the upper half-plane and let $(c_m)_{m \ge 0}$ be a sequence of complex numbers. Two hypotheses are imposed. First, for every $\tau \in \mathfrak{H}$ the family $m \mapsto c_m\, q^m$, where $q = e^{2\pi i \tau}$ is Mathlib's $q$-parameter `Function.Periodic.qParam 1` evaluated at $\tau$, is summable with sum $F(\tau)$; thus $F$ is everywhere given by a convergent power series in $q$ with no polar part and no negative-index terms. Second, $F$ is invariant under the Möbius action of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ on $\mathfrak{H}$: $F(\gamma \cdot \tau) = F(\tau)$ for all $\gamma \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ and all $\tau \in \mathfrak{H}$. The conclusion is that $c_m = 0$ for every index $m \ne 0$. Consequently $F$ is the constant function with value $c_0$. No holomorphy or growth condition on $F$ is assumed beyond the existence of the convergent $q$-expansion itself.
--
--   This is the weight-zero Liouville step: a modular function for the full level-one group which is holomorphic on $\mathfrak{H}$ and at the cusp is constant, here recorded as the vanishing of all higher $q$-expansion coefficients. It is used in the proof that the coefficients of the modular polynomial, viewed as functions on the upper half-plane, lie in the ring generated by $j$, via [`ModularCurve.mem_adjoin_jq_of_hasSum_of_slash_invariant`](thm.html#ModularCurve.mem_adjoin_jq_of_hasSum_of_slash_invariant).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_coeff_eq_zero_of_hasSum_of_slash_invariant.lean

import Mathlib.Analysis.Complex.UpperHalfPlane.Exp
import Mathlib.Analysis.Complex.UpperHalfPlane.MoebiusAction

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

theorem ModularCurve.coeff_eq_zero_of_hasSum_of_slash_invariant {F : UpperHalfPlane → ℂ} {c : ℕ → ℂ} (hF : ∀ τ : UpperHalfPlane, HasSum (fun m : ℕ => c m * Function.Periodic.qParam 1 (τ : ℂ) ^ m) (F τ)) (hinv : ∀ (γ : Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup (Fin 2) ℤ) (τ : UpperHalfPlane), F (γ • τ) = F τ) {m : ℕ} (hm : m ≠ 0) : c m = 0 := by sorry
